0..76 Comment "// Two rules of a nominal theory that overlap below an abstraction. A rule\'s"
77..153 Comment "// abstraction is one head at any depth, so the checker finds the pair there"
154..176 Comment "// as the kernel does."
177..179 Comment "//"
180..195 Comment "// - see: #1709"
197..275 Comment "/// `inner` rewrites the restriction inside `nu(bind a . nu(bind b . z()))` to"
276..355 Comment "/// `nu(bind a . w())`, a normal form, while `outer` rewrites the whole term to"
356..435 Comment "/// `z()`. The completion orients the two reducts into a rule of their own, and"
436..476 Comment "/// the kernel replays it from the pair."
